# How this build reaches Supabase.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.production`, paste the publishable key, and commit it.
# Vite reads it at build time and the deploy picks it up on the next push; with no
# file the site serves the versioned seed and the panel says there is nothing to
# sign in to, which is a working site rather than a broken one.
#
#     cp .env.production.example .env.production
#
# Both values are public by design. The project URL is already in this repository
# and the publishable key ships inside the site's own JavaScript bundle, where
# anybody can read it: security rests on row level security in the database, which
# `supabase/tests/row-level-security.sql` asserts. What must never go in here, or
# anywhere in this repository, is the **service role** key, which bypasses row
# level security entirely.
#
# The key is on the project's API keys page:
# https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/wqgmdjmdobgcrioxlhkl/settings/api-keys
#
# The alternative, and the cleaner one if whoever owns the repository is around:
# set `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` as repository variables under
# Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions. The deploy workflow already reads
# them, and then no key is committed at all. Setting them needs admin on the
# repository, which a collaborator on a personal repository cannot have.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://wqgmdjmdobgcrioxlhkl.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
